B.bPi=new A.kK("read_knowledge","Read your world directly, without searching it. Three resolutions, decided by the arguments, each paged:\n- **No arguments** \u2014 the shelf: every base you can read, with what each is for.\n- **`base`** \u2014 that base's entries, by title and length (no prose).\n- **`base` and `entry`** \u2014 that entry's chunks, in order. Add `query` to keep only chunks whose text contains it (SQLite LIKE, case-insensitive for ASCII); omit it to read the entry whole, a chunk-page at a time.\nEvery result starts with \"Page X of Y \xb7 N items\", so page on while X < Y. Prefer `ask_knowledge` when you have a question; prefer this when you want the material. What it returns is your author's own words and is authoritative.",B.bBl,!1,!0,!1,B.ja)
